The cart area shows the selected items efficently but it does not
allow you to change quantitys of values within the receipt. This is a
QOL feature that should be implemented. Please check 31-08-3.png, now
rows can be clicked to remove them from the cart

After platform testing it was found that windows does not launch the
pywebview, this can be solved by simply removing the extra
non-required flags. The next issue is that on Windows, Python path
locations do not work the same way on Windows and UNIX.

Take for example the following fs: files/ file123.txt libs/ lib.py
init.py

on Unix, if init.py imports a function from lib.py and that file
happens to look for the abspath of files/file123.txt, it will find it
with no problems.  This is because on UNIX, included files still use
the root working directory of the parent file.

However in Windows systems, the working directory of included
functions is actually in the same abspath as the included file. so if
the function from before ran on windows, it would look for
libs/files/file123.txt which does not exist..

This will require platform specific tuning.

